# compose/a770-sycl.env — the SYCL container envelope's host-specific values.
# Copy this file to compose/a770-sycl.env (gitignored) and edit it. harness/serve_compose.sh passes it to
# `docker compose --env-file`; a variable already exported by harness/env.sh wins over this file, so set here only
# what env.sh does not know: the image and the two DRM nodes / host group ids for THIS machine.
#
# The image: full-intel, NOT server-intel. server-intel ships llama-server only; full-intel copies build/bin/*
# so the one-shot llama-bench job (the speed rung) is in the same image. This is the SYCL sibling of the
# full-vulkan image; the A770 is DG2/Xe1 and runs the SYCL (oneAPI / Level Zero) path, unlike vLLM's XPU line.
#
# Pin the exact bytes by digest, never the floating tag: upstream can move a tag at any time, so the same name can
# hand a different image to another host. Pull once, read the fingerprint, and paste it here. Replace the tag
# below with your own digest after your first pull:
#   docker pull ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp:full-intel
#   docker inspect --format='{{index .RepoDigests 0}}' ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp:full-intel
# The first pull legitimately starts from the tag; `local-build.sh doctor` warns until this line carries a digest.
# A digest is a name that cannot be silently swapped, not a secret — safe to commit.
A770B_LLAMA_IMAGE=ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp:full-intel
# The A770's two DRM nodes by PCI BDF (not card0/renderD128: those names drift when the desktop moves).
# Find yours with: ls -l /dev/dri/by-path/   and   lspci -nn | grep -i vga
A770B_DRM_CARD=/dev/dri/by-path/pci-0000:0b:00.0-card
A770B_DRM_RENDER=/dev/dri/by-path/pci-0000:0b:00.0-render
# The host render and video group ids: `getent group render` and `getent group video` on THIS host.
# 105 and 39 are this workstation's; the next host will differ.
A770B_RENDER_GID=105
A770B_VIDEO_GID=39
# SYCL device selection (Level Zero). With only the A770's two DRM nodes passed into the container, the A770 is
# the only level-zero device, so `level_zero:gpu` names it. Use `level_zero:0` to pin by index if needed.
A770B_ONEAPI_DEVICE_SELECTOR=level_zero:gpu
#
# A770B_MODELS, A770B_PORT, A770B_API_KEY_FILE come from harness/env.sh (builder.env or the environment), so they
# are deliberately NOT set here — one source, not two. A770B_COMPOSE_FILE must point at compose/a770-sycl.yaml to
# select this envelope over the Vulkan one.
